{
  "url": "https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/08/08/the-abbey-road-cover-photography-session/",
  "type": "history",
  "slug": "the-abbey-road-cover-photography-session",
  "title": "8 August 1969: The Abbey Road cover photoshoot",
  "date": "1969-08-08",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>All four Beatles gathered at EMI Studios on the morning of Friday 8 August 1969 for one of the most famous photo shoots of their career. Photographer Iain Macmillan took the iconic image that adorned the front of their last-recorded album, <a href=\"/albums/abbey-road/\"><em>Abbey Road</em></a>. <span id=\"more-3218\"></span></p><p>Here is a photograph taken earlier in August 1969, showing the empty crossing.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/miscellany/abbey-road-empty-690808/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-11090\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"sync\" data-attachment-id=\"11090\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/miscellany/abbey-road-empty-690808/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/abbey-road-empty-690808.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"717,482\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Abbey Road, taken on the morning of The Beatles&amp;#8217; album cover shoot, 8 August 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/abbey-road-empty-690808.jpg\" src=\"/wp/media/abbey-road-empty-690808-580x389.jpg\" alt=\"Abbey Road, taken on the morning of the album cover shoot, 8 August 1969\" title=\"Abbey Road, taken on the morning of The Beatles' album cover shoot, 8 August 1969\" width=\"580\" height=\"389\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-11090\"></a></p><p>Iain Macmillan was a freelance photographer and a friend to <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> and <a href=\"/people/yoko-ono/\">Yoko Ono</a>. He used a Hasselblad camera with a 50mm lens, aperture f22, at 1/500 seconds.</p><p>Prior to the shoot, <a href=\"/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a> had sketched his ideas for the cover, to which Macmillan added a more detailed illustration.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/1969-photos/690808_abbey-road-sketch/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-8971\"><img decoding=\"sync\" data-attachment-id=\"8971\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690808_abbey-road-sketch/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road-sketch.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"401,437\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Sketch for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road-sketch.jpg\" src=\"/wp/media/690808_abbey-road-sketch.jpg\" alt=\"Sketch for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" title=\"Sketch for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" width=\"401\" height=\"437\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-8971\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road-sketch.jpg 401w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road-sketch-184x200.jpg 184w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 401px) 100vw, 401px\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></p><p>As the group waited outside the studio for the shoot to begin, <a href=\"/people/linda-mccartney/\">Linda McCartney</a> took a number of extra photographs.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/1969-photos/690808_abbey-road_01/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-8970\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIzMzEiIGhlaWdodD0iNDk2IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMzMxIDQ5NiI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"8970\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1969-photos/690808_abbey-road_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"331,496\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles prepare for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road_01.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/690808_abbey-road_01.jpg\" alt=\"The Beatles prepare for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" title=\"The Beatles prepare for the Abbey Road album cover photo shoot, 8 August 1969\" width=\"331\" height=\"496\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-8970\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road_01.jpg 331w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/690808_abbey-road_01-133x200.jpg 133w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 331px) 100vw, 331px\"></a></p><p>A policeman held up the traffic as Macmillan, from a stepladder positioned in the middle of the road, took six shots as the group walked across the zebra crossing just outside the studio.</p><p>The Beatles crossed the road a number of times while Macmillan photographed them. 8 August was a hot day in north London, and for four of the six photographs McCartney walked barefoot; for the other two he wore sandals.</p><blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\" data-width=\"550\" data-dnt=\"true\"><p lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://twitter.com/hashtag/OTD?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">#OTD</a> 1969, Abbey Road cover shoot: 'We're meant to be recording, not posing for Beatle pictures'- that's what we were thinking\" – John <a href=\"https://t.co/pspiOfUnyh\">pic.twitter.com/pspiOfUnyh</a></p><p>— The Beatles (@thebeatles) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/thebeatles/status/894925982930481153?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">August 8, 2017</a></p></blockquote><p></p><p>Shortly after the shoot, McCartney studied the transparencies and chose the fifth one for the album cover. It was the only one when all four Beatles were walking in time. It also satisfied The Beatles’ desire for the world to see them walking away from the studios they had spent so much of the last seven years inside.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/08/08/the-abbey-road-cover-photography-session/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-3218 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/alternative-images/alternative-abbey-road_01/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Picture one from the Abbey Road photography session (photo: Iain Macmillan)\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-960x960.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"70060\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/alternative-images/alternative-abbey-road_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,1000\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Picture one from the Abbey Road photography session (photo: Iain Macmillan)\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/alternative-abbey-road_01-960x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href